# Event App API

REST API for managing events and attendees built with Go, Gin, PostgreSQL and JWT authentication.

## Features

* User registration and login
* JWT authentication
* Event CRUD operations
* Event attendees management
* PostgreSQL database
* Database migrations
* Swagger documentation
* Docker support

## Tech Stack

* Go
* Gin
* PostgreSQL
* JWT
* Docker
* Swagger

## Project Structure

```text
back/
├── cmd/
│   ├── api/
│   └── migrate/
├── internal/
│   ├── database/
│   └── env/
├── docs/
├── go.mod
└── go.sum
```

## Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file inside:

```text
cmd/api/
```

Example:

```env
PORT=5623
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/event_app?sslmode=disable
JWT_SECRET=your-secret-key
```

## Running the Application

Install Air:

```bash
go install github.com/air-verse/air@latest
```

Navigate to:

```bash
cd cmd/api
```

Run:

```bash
air
```

API will be available at:

```text
http://localhost:5623
```

## Database Migrations

Create a migration:

```bash
migrate create -ext sql -dir ./cmd/migrate/migrations -seq create_attendees_table
```

Example migration:

`000001_create_attendees_table.up.sql`

```sql
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS attendees (
    id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    user_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
    event_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
    FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    FOREIGN KEY (event_id) REFERENCES events(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
);
```

`000001_create_attendees_table.down.sql`

```sql
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS attendees;
```

## Swagger

Install Swag:

```bash
go install github.com/swaggo/swag/cmd/swag@latest
```

Generate documentation:

```bash
swag init --dir cmd/api --parseDependency --parseInternal --parseDepth 1
```

Swagger UI:

```text
http://localhost:5623/swagger/index.html
```

## API Endpoints

### Authentication

```http
POST /api/v1/auth/register
POST /api/v1/auth/login
```

### Events

```http
GET    /api/v1/events
GET    /api/v1/events/:id
POST   /api/v1/events
PUT    /api/v1/events/:id
DELETE /api/v1/events/:id
```

### Attendees

```http
GET    /api/v1/events/:id/attendees
GET    /api/v1/attendees/:id/events
POST   /api/v1/events/:id/attendees/:userId
DELETE /api/v1/events/:id/attendees/:userId
```

## Authentication

Protected endpoints require:

```http
Authorization: Bearer <jwt-token>
```

## Status

Backend is functional and currently being expanded with a React frontend.
